TensorFlow defines the XNNPACK repository this build uses (LiteRT's own
definition is skipped: TensorFlow's comes first). This adds our XNNPACK patch
to it (patch_c_api.sh section 21). The hunk names the pinned archive, so a
TensorFlow that moves XNNPACK fails the fetch until the XNNPACK patch is
re-checked. Strip 0, like third_party/tensorflow/tensorflow.patch. Against
TensorFlow faa06da43657488c1f7479289d11d15e03a15ba1 (LiteRT-LM v0.20.0
TENSORFLOW_REF), XNNPACK 08cc38b61f7589f84e91c6e343e0f130ae3279ca.

--- third_party/xla/third_party/xnnpack/workspace.bzl	2026-11-25 04:45:21
+++ third_party/xla/third_party/xnnpack/workspace.bzl	2026-11-25 04:45:21
@@ -24,5 +24,6 @@
         sha256 = "1c94d80ff3069b3510e54b41a2c82729a4053724a682fcb09840af296dcaa07c",
         strip_prefix = "XNNPACK-08cc38b61f7589f84e91c6e343e0f130ae3279ca",
         urls = tf_mirror_urls("https://github.com/google/XNNPACK/archive/08cc38b61f7589f84e91c6e343e0f130ae3279ca.zip"),
+        patch_file = ["@//:flutter_gemma_xnnpack_pf32_sme2_apple.patch"],
     )
     # LINT.ThenChange(//tensorflow/lite/tools/cmake/modules/xnnpack.cmake)
